dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Node / Next.js ────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
npm-debug.log*
.vercel

# ─── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# ─── Docs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no tracked `docs/` any more. Jelena's decision, 2026-07-31: the repo
# is meant to be read the way any GitHub repo is read — README.md for users and
# developers — and the working documents belong with the tooling that uses
# them, in `.claude/rules/`.
#
# They are still IN GIT, and that matters: `docs/` was once ignored wholesale,
# which hid PLAN, API, MCP, AUTH, VECTORS, MANUAL, TODO and CONTINUE, so a clone
# had broken links and none of the reasoning travelled with the code. Moving
# them is not the same as hiding them.
#
# `docs/` is now entirely untracked, and that is safe *because* the documents
# moved into `.claude/rules/` — the old bug was ignoring the folder while the
# reasoning still lived in it. What is here now is Jelena's own:
#
#   docs/SESSIONS.md  the readable summary of where the project stands. Her
#                     decision, 2026-07-31: "the repo is not the place for the
#                     summary of our sessions." Update it at the end of a
#                     session; it is written for her, not for a clone.
#   docs/jelena/      hers, off-limits — never read, never cite
#   docs/ops/         her machines and network: private, but written for a
#                     session to execute, so read it when the task is her laptops
docs/
docs/jelena/

# ─── The working documents ─────────────────────────────────
# Jelena's decision, 2026-07-31: the repository carries the code and README.md,
# and nothing about how the work was done. The documents live in
# `.claude/rules/` on her machine; only the map of them is tracked.
#
# Known cost, accepted: a fresh clone has no reasoning in it, so the machine
# holding these files is the one that can continue the work.
.claude/rules/*
!.claude/rules/SUMMARY.md
# Infrastructure plans for Jelena's own machines — her home network, what runs
# on it, how it is exposed. Private, but NOT off-limits: unlike docs/jelena/
# these were written for a future session to execute, so they must stay
# readable. That is the whole reason they are here and not there.
docs/ops/
# .claude/rules/other_agent.md is deliberately NOT listed: it is already tracked, so a rule
# here would do nothing but mislead. It is excluded from the *public* repo by
# the sync script instead — see .claude/rules/DEPLOY-HF.md.
# Next.js incremental build cache. Regenerated on every build, so tracking it
# means every `npm run build` dirties git status and every commit carries noise.
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
